        "decode_reencode_identity": true,
        "decoded_response_text": "```python\n\"\"\"\nModule: streaming_parser.py\nDescription:\n    This module implements a robust, memory-efficient streaming parser for\n    processing large-scale JSON data streams. It demonstrates the concept\n    of incremental parsing, where data is processed in chunks as it arrives,\n    rather than loading the entire dataset into memory at once. This is\n    critical for handling datasets that exceed available RAM, such as\n    log files, financial transaction streams, or IoT sensor data.\n\n    The implementation includes:\n    1. A custom JSON tokenizer that handles nested structures incrementally.\n    2. A state machine to track the current parsing context.\n    3. Error handling for malformed JSON structures.\n    4. Performance benchmarking utilities.\n    5. A comprehensive test suite demonstrating various edge cases.\n\n    Key Design Principles:\n    - Memory Efficiency: Only the current chunk and necessary context are\n      held in memory.\n    - Fault Tolerance: Malformed data does not crash the parser; errors are\n      logged and the parser attempts to resynchronize.\n    - Extensibility: The parser can be extended to support other formats\n      (e.g., CSV, XML) by implementing the same interface",
